WEBVTT

01:35.670 --> 01:38.240
We were right to get out of there quickly.

01:38.830 --> 01:42.220
We'll take the Slayer Candidate 
position another time.

01:42.740 --> 01:45.490
If we can stay alive, that is.

01:50.240 --> 01:52.920
They hacked the <i>Archimedes</i>?

01:53.740 --> 01:56.700
You've really done it now, Catfish.

02:18.130 --> 02:20.230
That was too much for you? Pathetic.

02:20.230 --> 02:21.660
What was that, eyeball turtle?!

02:21.660 --> 02:22.820
Who are you calling pathetic?!

02:22.820 --> 02:24.660
We're out!

02:29.990 --> 02:30.930
Bam!

02:30.930 --> 02:32.080
Viole!

02:32.080 --> 02:33.450
Guys!

02:34.690 --> 02:37.260
Everyone escaped, including the hostages.

02:37.260 --> 02:38.540
Xia Xia!

02:40.070 --> 02:41.170
I'm glad you're okay.

02:49.900 --> 02:51.730
<i>Don't just stand there!</i>

02:51.990 --> 02:53.730
Hurry up and get in!

02:56.170 --> 02:57.500
Hold it right there.

02:58.240 --> 03:00.150
Take one step...

03:01.100 --> 03:03.070
and I'll kill everyone.

03:06.950 --> 03:09.370
<i>Lero Ro, the Rankers found us!</i>

03:09.370 --> 03:10.370
Huh?

03:10.720 --> 03:13.530
<i>What should we do? The kids 
are already at their limit!</i>

03:14.630 --> 03:17.600
There's only one thing to do!

03:18.890 --> 03:22.510
Damn it! This is why I didn't want to do this!

03:24.380 --> 03:25.760
<i>Stop!</i>

03:28.020 --> 03:29.520
<i>Emergency orders!</i>

03:32.170 --> 03:34.240
<i>Abandon the Thorn and head back.</i>

03:34.240 --> 03:37.210
<i>Don't do anything else. 
Just head back. That's all.</i>

03:47.050 --> 03:50.000
What are you standing around for? Hurry up!

03:50.860 --> 03:54.350
You seem to have summoned 
an unbelievable monster.

03:54.350 --> 03:55.250
What?

03:55.880 --> 03:58.220
This wasn't a bad fight,

03:58.620 --> 04:01.590
but you won't get a second chance, rat.

04:05.250 --> 04:06.960
<i>Ro, get in!</i>

04:08.950 --> 04:10.660
How long?

04:10.660 --> 04:13.690
How long have you been keeping an eye on us,

04:14.060 --> 04:17.650
Po Bidau Gustang, head of 
one of the Ten Families?

04:17.970 --> 04:21.220
Are you the one who gave 
the Thorn to FUG, too?

04:21.220 --> 04:23.400
I know nothing.

04:27.560 --> 04:31.420
I just came to take charge 
of the Workshop Battle and

04:31.420 --> 04:35.420
added sanctions to maintain 
the fairness of the games.

04:36.670 --> 04:40.670
Now, the winners must be given their prize.

05:03.400 --> 05:07.410
<b></b>The Winning Team of the Tournament Is
<b>Ramenmaru</b>

05:07.410 --> 05:11.410
<b></b>The Winning Team of the Tournament Is
<b> Ramenmaru</b>

05:07.850 --> 05:11.410
<i>Humans are truly ambiguous creatures.</i>

05:11.410 --> 05:14.410
<b></b>The Winning Team of the Tournament Is
<b> Ramenmaru</b>

05:14.660 --> 05:19.420
<i>They rebel when they learn there's 
someone looking down on them.</i>

05:19.420 --> 05:25.920
<i>But the moment they learn it brings 
about peace, they conform to the system.</i>

05:25.920 --> 05:30.680
<i>In that regard, the people of 
the Tower are truly human-like.</i>

05:31.140 --> 05:34.680
Merchant groups hate to incur losses.

05:35.450 --> 05:38.540
But this will be quite a blow to FUG.

05:38.540 --> 05:41.690
It will complicate their 
deal with the Workshop.

05:42.750 --> 05:50.500
<i>So, who is the true prince of Jahad who 
will hold the final test of the Tower?</i>

05:50.980 --> 05:52.700
You're impatient, aren't you?

05:53.130 --> 05:56.080
You'll have to wait and 
watch a little longer.

06:01.710 --> 06:05.290
His adventure has just begun.

06:05.290 --> 06:07.720
Don't go too crazy, everyone.

06:07.720 --> 06:09.350
More!

06:09.350 --> 06:10.970
There's not enough food.

06:10.970 --> 06:13.540
I'm gonna drink like a fish today!

06:13.540 --> 06:15.600
Let's have another toast!

06:15.600 --> 06:16.900
Yeah!

06:17.550 --> 06:19.310
Ready, and...

06:19.310 --> 06:21.500
Cheers!

06:40.190 --> 06:41.170
Welcome back.

06:54.190 --> 06:55.560
Where are the others?

06:58.090 --> 07:00.440
Is everyone here?

07:01.130 --> 07:04.440
Yes. Horyang, Viole, and everyone else.

07:05.330 --> 07:06.690
I see.

07:07.640 --> 07:11.430
Then bring me something to eat, 
as long as it's not your cooking.

07:12.270 --> 07:13.700
Rude.

07:16.090 --> 07:18.950
The invincible Wangnan has 
made a complete recovery!

07:19.180 --> 07:21.990
You're finally awake, hero?

07:21.990 --> 07:27.060
I wish I could say that I am,
but honestly, I don't remember a thing.

07:27.060 --> 07:30.400
Seriously, thank you. You did an amazing job.

07:30.400 --> 07:32.970
Who knows what would've 
happened without you?

07:32.970 --> 07:34.890
Yo, did you hear that?

07:34.890 --> 07:36.610
You should stay in bed a little longer.

07:36.610 --> 07:37.720
What was that?!

07:37.720 --> 07:41.600
Apparently this is a resort 
owned by the wolhaiksong.

07:42.150 --> 07:44.860
A Ranker we know is looking after us.

07:45.680 --> 07:47.680
You should take it easy and rest.

07:48.110 --> 07:50.060
Huh.

07:50.060 --> 07:51.750
I hope you'll keep looking out for Bam, too.

07:51.750 --> 07:54.340
Huh? What do you mean?

07:54.340 --> 07:56.640
Aren't you going to climb 
the Tower with him?

07:57.960 --> 07:59.980
I wish I could.

08:00.730 --> 08:05.190
But we came back down after 
becoming D-Rank Regulars.

08:05.690 --> 08:08.380
We'll be leaving in three 
days to take a test.

08:09.030 --> 08:10.380
No way...

08:10.380 --> 08:16.390
I know. It's incredibly disappointing, 
but we've got our own goals.

08:16.890 --> 08:18.890
We have to keep moving, you know?

08:24.900 --> 08:28.150
So catch up to us quickly.

08:29.760 --> 08:34.500
Let's hone our skills so we can trade 
a few blows the next time we meet.

08:35.380 --> 08:38.650
Go on. Show your friends you're okay.

08:38.650 --> 08:39.650
Right.

08:40.050 --> 08:41.410
Hey!

08:41.670 --> 08:43.410
Help...

08:43.680 --> 08:47.650
It's a miracle he survived his 
heart being pierced at all,

08:47.650 --> 08:49.920
but he's already this well after a day.

08:50.150 --> 08:52.550
Right? Isn't he amazing?

08:52.550 --> 08:54.700
My chirpy is immortal!

08:54.700 --> 08:56.800
Isn't that just the coolest?

08:56.800 --> 09:00.440
Yeah. I wasn't impressed 
by him at first, but...

09:02.420 --> 09:04.460
There's something more to him.

09:06.740 --> 09:08.340
Maybe I'll look into it.

09:11.790 --> 09:14.780
Hatzling, this series of events...

09:14.780 --> 09:16.630
I won't tell anyone.

09:16.630 --> 09:21.450
Not even I'm interested in tormenting 
my cute little brother's friends.

09:21.940 --> 09:24.280
It'll probably shorten my lifespan, though.

09:24.280 --> 09:25.460
What?!

09:25.770 --> 09:26.460
Huh?

09:26.460 --> 09:27.310
Nothing.

09:28.090 --> 09:29.970
Majex, how's the vice captain?

09:30.320 --> 09:32.190
We can't get in touch with him.

09:32.190 --> 09:37.510
He's probably passed out drunk 
or chasing women somewhere.

09:37.960 --> 09:40.730
It would be wise to give up 
on trying to meet with him.

09:41.350 --> 09:42.730
I see.

09:42.730 --> 09:45.520
Then perhaps we'll head back 
after seeing them off.

09:45.520 --> 09:48.010
Aren't they taking the D-Rank test next?

09:48.010 --> 09:51.230
And that test involves... what, again?

09:51.950 --> 09:55.630
The hell train bound for the hidden floor.

09:57.410 --> 10:00.670
Fantastic. Sounds like there will be...

10:01.760 --> 10:03.810
plenty more interesting things happening.

10:27.020 --> 10:33.400
Did you come to help me loosen up because 
you were worried I might be out of shape?

10:33.900 --> 10:36.700
Well, Karaka?

10:39.120 --> 10:42.300
Thank you for coming, Master.

10:46.760 --> 10:50.540
You pulled quite the 
stunt on the <i>Archimedes</i>.

10:50.840 --> 10:53.510
I didn't expect you to go 
after the Slayer Candidate.

10:55.110 --> 10:56.910
Why did you do that?

10:57.800 --> 11:03.050
It was the most efficient way 
to achieve our greatest desire.

11:03.050 --> 11:05.820
Don't you mean "your" greatest desire?

11:07.140 --> 11:11.030
One of the Elders who 
plotted this with you died.

11:12.130 --> 11:16.320
I wanted them to remain alive so they 
could testify about these events.

11:17.080 --> 11:20.270
Who knew you had the power 
to shake the Elders?

11:21.070 --> 11:22.820
You've become horrifyingly strong.

11:23.670 --> 11:26.330
You're the one who's truly 
horrifying, Master.

11:26.330 --> 11:30.140
You knew what was happening, didn't you?

11:30.990 --> 11:32.820
You used our plan against us

11:32.820 --> 11:38.240
in order to diminish our influence and 
move the Thorn and Viole to a safe place.

11:38.240 --> 11:40.080
What is your ultimate goal?

11:40.080 --> 11:43.260
I should warn you,

11:44.020 --> 11:47.720
Viole has grown far more 
than you can imagine.

11:47.720 --> 11:50.270
In the not-so-distant future...

11:50.850 --> 11:52.870
He might come for my head?

11:54.380 --> 11:57.110
Don't say I didn't warn you. Later.

12:07.050 --> 12:08.370
Endorsi.

12:09.140 --> 12:10.160
You're late!

12:10.160 --> 12:11.370
Sorry.

12:11.370 --> 12:12.850
I thought...

12:14.500 --> 12:16.900
<b>Meet me at the plaza at 14:00 tomorrow.</b>

12:14.500 --> 12:16.900
<b>If you don't show up, I'll kill you!</b>

12:14.870 --> 12:17.000
you hadn't seen my message.

12:17.000 --> 12:19.130
Hurry! We'll be late!

12:19.760 --> 12:22.000
It's obvious that you're tailing them.

12:23.140 --> 12:28.010
What kind of lowlifes spy on 
people's private lives, anyway?

12:28.800 --> 12:31.180
We're not spying! We're observing!

12:31.180 --> 12:35.770
Y-Yeah! The eyeball turtle is 
trying to kidnap the black turtle!

12:35.770 --> 12:37.940
Yeah! The idea that they'd 
go on a date is absurd!

12:38.430 --> 12:40.390
Don't say I didn't warn you.

12:40.840 --> 12:43.380
Try not to get killed by Endorsi.

12:44.200 --> 12:45.670
Blue turtle, where are you going?

12:45.050 --> 12:49.210
<i>I came because I was worried, but if he's 
got someone watching him, he should be fine.</i>

12:45.670 --> 12:47.220
Keep your voice down!

12:46.340 --> 12:48.550
Damn it! Let me go on a date 
with the princess, too!

12:48.550 --> 12:49.200
Are you listening?!

12:52.360 --> 12:53.710
Sorry to keep you waiting.

12:54.260 --> 12:55.880
How's Viole?

12:55.880 --> 12:57.290
He's fine.

12:57.290 --> 13:00.850
Not even that reckless princess 
would cause trouble now.

13:00.850 --> 13:03.720
I can't believe he's on a date 
with a princess of Jahad.

13:03.720 --> 13:06.220
That isn't enough to surprise me anymore.

13:06.820 --> 13:09.680
So, are we disbanding?

13:10.750 --> 13:12.730
You're teaming up with them, right?

13:13.150 --> 13:13.980
Yeah.

13:14.900 --> 13:17.340
But I don't intend to disband our team.

13:18.050 --> 13:22.070
I want you to work toward 
achieving another goal.

13:22.070 --> 13:22.980
What other goal?

13:23.630 --> 13:26.240
Find Rachel and her allies.

13:27.950 --> 13:30.970
What happened to Gyetang 
and Dan wasn't your fault.

13:31.390 --> 13:33.790
You found the friend you were looking for.

13:33.790 --> 13:36.030
There's no reason to keep focusing on her.

13:36.030 --> 13:37.000
No, I have to.

13:37.250 --> 13:42.750
For them, and most of all, 
I have to do it for myself.

13:42.750 --> 13:47.260
So nothing important to me breaks again.

13:56.880 --> 14:00.370
That's fine with me. Leaving things as they 
are now leaves a bad aftertaste, anyway.

14:00.370 --> 14:02.270
Hey, that's not your decision to make.

14:02.270 --> 14:06.070
Novick, I want you to lead your team.

14:06.950 --> 14:10.130
Well, if you insist.

14:10.130 --> 14:14.290
Given our objective, how should 
we find the rest of our members?

14:14.730 --> 14:16.530
Don't worry about that.

14:20.490 --> 14:21.540
I'm surprised.

14:23.480 --> 14:25.960
They projected an image onto a huge wall.

14:25.960 --> 14:27.300
You mean the screen.

14:27.300 --> 14:30.890
Sorry. That was my first time seeing a movie.

14:31.810 --> 14:32.800
Oh...

14:33.190 --> 14:38.810
<i>I insisted we go on a date and watch that 
boring movie because of our promise...</i>

14:39.460 --> 14:42.890
<i>But I'm not even sure this 
can be called a date.</i>

14:43.300 --> 14:45.430
<i>What am I doing?</i>

14:45.830 --> 14:48.070
That protagonist was amazing.

14:48.070 --> 14:49.850
You mean from that movie?

14:49.850 --> 14:53.220
Yes. The way they became stronger

14:53.220 --> 14:57.080
so they could risk their life to protect 
their loved ones was awesome.

14:57.590 --> 14:59.210
What are you talking about?

14:59.210 --> 15:02.580
You're way better than that made-up story.

15:03.140 --> 15:08.420
I'm not better. All I ever did was...

15:11.120 --> 15:12.840
I only tried as hard as I could

15:13.580 --> 15:19.600
because I thought becoming 
stronger was my only option.

15:19.920 --> 15:23.410
But in the end, I needed all 
kinds of help from others.

15:23.410 --> 15:26.890
What? You should expect people to help you.

15:27.860 --> 15:29.930
Give and receive help.

15:30.250 --> 15:35.880
Strength exists to prove 
you're worthy of that.

15:35.880 --> 15:37.130
You got that?

15:38.370 --> 15:41.120
You're amazing, Endorsi.

15:42.370 --> 15:46.970
I missed this feeling.

15:48.270 --> 15:53.890
<i>I see. I was desperate 
to see this face again.</i>

15:55.210 --> 15:55.950
Let's go.

15:55.950 --> 15:57.640
Huh? But we still...

15:58.650 --> 16:00.960
Come on. We're going 
somewhere we can be alone.

16:02.140 --> 16:04.600
Wait, black turtle!

16:11.780 --> 16:13.690
You don't want to shop?

16:13.690 --> 16:16.520
I'll use your Pocket to go 
on a shopping spree later.

16:16.880 --> 16:17.870
Very well.

16:18.100 --> 16:22.620
You're free now, right? 
What are you going to do?

16:23.790 --> 16:25.210
Climb the Tower.

16:26.110 --> 16:28.540
Are you really going to look for her?

16:28.540 --> 16:30.360
What are you going to do when you find her?

16:30.880 --> 16:32.430
I'm not sure.

16:32.430 --> 16:34.200
Forget I asked.

16:34.780 --> 16:39.890
Why am I reminding you of another 
girl while we're on a date?

16:40.200 --> 16:41.100
A date?

16:41.640 --> 16:44.350
What? Don't tell me you don't remember!

16:44.350 --> 16:46.680
We agreed to go on a date!

16:46.680 --> 16:48.400
I-I'm sorry.

16:48.400 --> 16:50.910
This is my first date, too.

16:50.910 --> 16:53.370
I don't know what to expect.

16:55.670 --> 16:58.010
Then I'll show you.

17:04.520 --> 17:09.410
Dates are for creating 
unforgettable memories.

17:10.730 --> 17:16.180
You'd better not forget a single thing 
about me before the next time we meet.

17:16.850 --> 17:18.430
This is a date?

17:18.430 --> 17:20.780
Uh... Well, no...

17:20.780 --> 17:23.630
But whatever. Let's go shopping.

17:23.630 --> 17:25.690
I'm gonna shop till I drop!

17:30.960 --> 17:33.070
I'm not looking forward to leaving tomorrow.

17:33.330 --> 17:35.570
We'll meet again once we're D-Rank.

17:35.870 --> 17:38.380
I'll get stronger by then.

17:39.350 --> 17:40.330
Right.

17:40.890 --> 17:45.580
I guess I could say I'm disappointed
I didn't get to see Urek before I left.

17:46.150 --> 17:48.830
I wanted to hear about the 
world outside the Tower.

17:49.270 --> 17:53.170
We'll definitely run into 
him if we become stronger.

17:53.170 --> 17:57.520
Then let's leave this weak 
little blue turtle here.

17:57.520 --> 17:58.840
What was that, gator?

17:59.140 --> 18:02.240
What exactly did you do during 
the Workshop Battle, huh?

18:02.240 --> 18:04.600
All you did was run off with the item!

18:04.600 --> 18:06.430
Quit your complaining, gator!

18:06.430 --> 18:07.600
I'll kill you!

18:07.600 --> 18:10.360
Gator, gator, gator!

18:09.090 --> 18:10.360
Viole.

18:10.890 --> 18:12.610
Do you have a minute?

18:13.220 --> 18:15.610
He's been asleep this whole time.

18:16.410 --> 18:18.620
You don't know why?

18:18.620 --> 18:23.540
All I can say is that the fiendish power 
that was inside Ilmar has vanished.

18:23.540 --> 18:24.620
Vanished?

18:24.990 --> 18:28.760
Cassano took Ilmar's devil.

18:28.760 --> 18:32.630
Does that mean he has two now?

18:32.630 --> 18:36.510
It's more accurate to say he's complete.

18:37.580 --> 18:40.760
He's probably way stronger than me now.

18:40.760 --> 18:44.510
Maybe even stronger than Viole.

18:45.530 --> 18:47.860
Wangnan, do the others know about this?

18:47.860 --> 18:49.270
No.

18:49.870 --> 18:52.480
I don't want to upset the others yet.

18:53.270 --> 18:56.650
We need to find Cassano as soon as possible.

18:56.650 --> 18:58.570
I'm worried about Emily, too.

18:58.570 --> 19:00.150
What's wrong with Emily?

19:00.750 --> 19:03.290
We haven't been able to use 
her for the past few days.

19:03.290 --> 19:06.390
Emily is a self-aware Ignition Weapon.

19:06.390 --> 19:07.290
What?

19:07.660 --> 19:12.830
Until now, Emily was convinced she 
was a human and kept locked away,

19:12.830 --> 19:16.170
but Cassano removed her protections.

19:16.500 --> 19:20.430
Something terrible will happen unless 
he's stopped before Emily awakens.

19:20.430 --> 19:21.930
Seriously?

19:22.280 --> 19:26.430
The Workshop Battle just ended, and we're 
already dealing with a bunch of problems?

19:27.030 --> 19:29.900
Khun, why don't we ask her?

19:32.370 --> 19:34.190
So, what are your conditions?

19:35.730 --> 19:37.690
That's the first thing you have to say?

19:40.030 --> 19:43.220
We're looking for a man 
named Beniamino Cassano.

19:43.220 --> 19:48.700
If you'll tell us how to find him, 
you can come with us again.

19:49.950 --> 19:54.730
The special D-Rank Regular 
test held on the 35th floor...

19:55.110 --> 19:56.530
The hell train.

19:57.630 --> 20:00.220
If you get on that train, 
you'll find Cassano.

20:00.220 --> 20:03.550
I see. Thanks, Hwaryun.

20:04.560 --> 20:05.320
Viole.

20:06.610 --> 20:09.310
Ha Jinsung asked me to 
deliver a message to you.

20:10.910 --> 20:13.530
"If you want to find happiness, 
then get stronger."

20:13.930 --> 20:19.550
"And deliver a blow to the 
higher-ups who put you in danger."

20:20.290 --> 20:24.490
The 35th floor, huh? That's pretty far away.

20:24.490 --> 20:27.770
I've heard of the hell train.

20:27.770 --> 20:31.740
They say only a handful of passengers 
make it to the end alive.

20:31.740 --> 20:33.530
But we've gotta do it, right?

20:34.530 --> 20:36.450
We're doing this for our friend.

20:36.860 --> 20:40.260
You guys are stupid strong. 
Don't be such cowards.

20:40.870 --> 20:42.260
Wangnan...

20:43.170 --> 20:44.230
Brat.

20:44.230 --> 20:44.840
Yeah!

20:44.840 --> 20:45.290
Ow!

20:45.290 --> 20:46.000
Excuse me.

20:47.150 --> 20:49.660
Before we leave, I have a request.

20:52.340 --> 20:54.270
Looks like it's finally over.

20:59.560 --> 21:03.280
But a new story will begin before long.

21:04.390 --> 21:08.280
Not even a Guide can control her.

21:09.140 --> 21:12.290
Like you, she is highly 
unusual within the Tower.

21:12.710 --> 21:15.200
Something that can change the tower.

21:15.600 --> 21:18.870
If you were to stand before her again,

21:19.320 --> 21:22.800
what choice would you make, Bam?

21:25.260 --> 21:26.550
Okay. Let's go.

21:29.490 --> 21:30.180
Yeah.

21:31.010 --> 21:35.020
<b>Episode 26</b>

21:31.010 --> 21:35.020
<b>The Dawn of Departure</b>

23:07.520 --> 23:08.600
We're here.

23:17.700 --> 23:19.580
We've been waiting for you.

23:20.980 --> 23:26.340
I thought something had happened to you 
on the <i>Archimedes</i> since you took so long.

23:26.820 --> 23:27.890
Nothing happened.

23:27.890 --> 23:30.520
I simply failed to bring along an ally.

23:30.900 --> 23:33.090
Could you show us the object?

23:35.930 --> 23:37.850
Then let's go...

23:38.120 --> 23:40.240
and save this Tower.

23:41.510 --> 23:44.770
<i>Tower of God</i> season two is now over.

23:45.110 --> 23:48.560
Thank you for watching!

